CAT = "cpatcpPassive"; SEG = "PAL"
Q = [
("Nina invests $30,000 cash in a partnership, is personally liable for $20,000 of its recourse debt, and has a $15,000 share of nonrecourse debt that is not qualified real estate financing. Her amount at risk is:",
 "$50,000", ["$65,000", "$30,000", "$45,000"],
 "Amounts at risk are cash and property contributed plus debts the partner is personally liable for (section 465(b)). Ordinary nonrecourse debt is excluded: $30,000 + $20,000 = $50,000.", 50000),
("For an activity of holding real estate, which debt counts as at risk even though no one is personally liable for it?",
 "A bank's nonrecourse mortgage", ["The seller's nonrecourse note", "A promoter's nonrecourse loan", "A loan from a fellow investor"],
 "Qualified nonrecourse financing, borrowed from a commercial lender or government and secured by the real property, counts as at risk (section 465(b)(6)). Seller and promoter financing does not qualify."),
("A loss passed through from a partnership is tested against the loss limits in which order?",
 "Basis, at-risk, then passive", ["Passive, at-risk, then basis", "At-risk, basis, then passive", "Basis, passive, then at-risk"],
 "A loss must first fit within the partner's basis, then the amount at risk, and only then is it tested under the passive activity rules. A loss can be suspended at each step."),
("Kai has three passive activities: A with $12,000 of income, B with a $20,000 loss and C with a $5,000 loss. None is rental real estate. His passive losses allowed this year total:",
 "$12,000", ["$25,000", "$13,000", "$0"],
 "Passive losses offset passive income only. The $25,000 of losses is allowed up to the $12,000 of passive income, and $13,000 is suspended.", 12000),
("Kai's passive activities B (a $20,000 loss) and C (a $5,000 loss) produce $13,000 of suspended loss this year after offsetting $12,000 of passive income. The suspended loss allocated to B is:",
 "$10,400", ["$13,000", "$8,000", "$6,500"],
 "Suspended losses are allocated in proportion to each loss activity's loss: $13,000 x $20,000 / $25,000 = $10,400.", 10400),
("Lia sells her entire interest in a passive activity to an unrelated buyer in a fully taxable sale for a $4,000 gain. The activity has $15,000 of suspended losses, and she has no other passive income. The net loss she may use against her wages and other income is:",
 "$11,000", ["$15,000", "$4,000", "$0"],
 "A fully taxable disposition to an unrelated party frees all suspended losses (section 469(g)). The $15,000 first absorbs the $4,000 gain, leaving an $11,000 net loss.", 11000),
("A taxpayer sells her whole interest in a passive activity to her brother. The activity's suspended losses are:",
 "Held until he sells to an outsider", ["Deducted in full this year", "Added to the brother's basis", "Lost permanently"],
 "When the buyer is related under section 267(b), the suspended losses stay with the seller and are freed only when the related buyer disposes of the interest to an unrelated person."),
("When an owner gives away an interest in a passive activity that has suspended losses, the losses are:",
 "Added to the donee's basis", ["Deducted by the donor now", "Passed to the donee as losses", "Deducted over 15 years"],
 "On a gift, section 469(j)(6) adds the suspended losses to the basis of the interest given, and no one deducts them as losses."),
("A taxpayer dies holding a passive activity with $30,000 of suspended losses. Its adjusted basis just before death was $50,000 and its value at death was $70,000. The suspended loss deductible on the final return is:",
 "$10,000", ["$30,000", "$20,000", "$0"],
 "At death the suspended loss is allowed only to the extent it exceeds the basis step-up (section 469(g)(2)): $30,000 - ($70,000 - $50,000) = $10,000.", 10000),
("Under the regulations, an individual materially participates in an activity if, among other tests, she works in it for more than:",
 "500 hours in the year", ["100 hours in the year", "250 hours in the year", "750 hours in the year"],
 "Temporary Regulation 1.469-5T lists seven tests; the first is more than 500 hours of participation during the year. 750 hours is the real estate professional test."),
("To treat her rental real estate as nonpassive, a real estate professional must work more than 750 hours in real property businesses in which she materially participates and also:",
 "Spend over half her work time there", ["Own at least 10% of each rental", "Earn under $100,000 of wages", "Hold a real estate license"],
 "Section 469(c)(7)(B) requires both more than half of her personal services and more than 750 hours in real property trades or businesses. No license is required."),
("Sara's share of an S corporation loss is $30,000. Her stock basis is $24,000, she has no debt basis, her amount at risk is $18,000, and she does not materially participate and has no passive income. The loss suspended by the passive activity rules is:",
 "$18,000", ["$24,000", "$30,000", "$6,000"],
 "Basis allows $24,000 ($6,000 suspended), the at-risk rules allow $18,000 ($6,000 more suspended), and the passive rules then suspend all $18,000 left.", 18000),
]
